# Two effect lines run as one group. The print finishes at once and the sleep
# parks its side, so every side is waiting: the first idle point, where the
# pool runs. The report's call is certain to follow the sleep and names
# nothing local, so it is lifted and forced there. `ahead_forced` counts it.
import "std/time"

fn spin 0 acc
  acc

fn spin n acc
  spin (n - 1) (acc + n % 7)

print "start"
sleep 1 .> (_ -> print "made") .> (_ -> print "report: {spin 1000 0}")
